{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\np='probe_level7.py'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"A.run_program('s5i5',probe)\\\",\\\"if __name__ == '__main__':\\\\n    A.run_program('s5i5',probe)\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > level7_verified.md <<'EOF'\n# Level 7 reproduced observations\n\n\"'`python gkm_try.py` initially returned levels=6, moves=177, replay_ok=True.\nThe final composed player returns levels=7, moves=224, replay_ok=True.\n`candidate_joint_staging_level7.json` preserves the complete 224-action path.\nThe supervisor checkpoint was only read.\n\nReproduction probes use the public frame, clone, actions, step, terminal and\nlevels_completed API, with perception.py components and action deltas.\n\n- `probe_rotations7.py`: root, middle and distal rotations affect their\n  descendants. Greedy tip alignment alone stalls at level 6.\n- `probe_complete7.py`: retracting colour 10 permits colour 8 to rotate,\n  clearing the vertical lane at x=13. The linked arm crosses the opening\n  centred at y=40, turns its retracted distal joint at x=7, raises the tip\n  to y=16, then extends it to the cross at (25,16). This partial alignment\n  leaves reward unchanged. Clearing colour 8 from the upper lane and\n  aligning the other tip with (22,7) completes the level.\n- `probe_joint7.py`: at the left staging point, two distal rotation clicks\n  produce the upward configuration; a third returns to the leftward one.\n- `save_candidate_level7.py`: reproduces the final shorter staging with\n  two early colour-8 rotations and the existing alignment leg as the suffix.\n\n`play_level_7` only composes the new general colour-control staging leg and\n`align_marked_bar_tips`. The staging leg detects panels from the frame,\nchecks its bounded sequence on a clone, and requires a successful alignment\nproof before committing. Earlier levels were not edited.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
